`Metric.__call__` in `keras/src/metrics/metric.py` directly does `self.update_state(*args, **kwargs)`. The test constructs a `BinaryAccuracy`, and `BinaryAccuracy` in `accuracy_metrics.py` inherits from `reduction_metrics.MeanMetricWrapper` without defining its own `update_state`. Therefore normal method resolution sends that call to `MeanMetricWrapper.update_state` in `keras/src/metrics/reduction_metrics.py`. That wrapper uses the stored `binary_accuracy` function, but the dispatched `update_state` implementation itself is the one defined on `MeanMetricWrapper`.

